  "notes": "USAGE:\n{目|め}を{伏|ふ}せる describes lowering the eyes to avoid eye contact. It often conveys emotions such as shame, shyness, sadness, or respect. It is frequently used in literary descriptions and narratives.\n\nThe verb {伏|ふ}せる is ichidan: {伏|ふ}せる → {伏|ふ}せない → {伏|ふ}せた → {伏|ふ}せて.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {目|め}を{逸|そ}らす (to avert one's eyes — more active avoidance)\n- {俯|うつむ}く (to hang one's head — involves tilting the whole head down)\n- {目|め}を{落|お}とす (to drop one's gaze — similar but slightly more literary)",
